<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Oakfields year loss narrows.</title>
<headline>Oakfields year loss narrows.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended July 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     2.43 loss   vs 6.17 loss</p>
<p>    Attrib loss	     2.43	  vs 6.17</p>
<p>    Operating loss	  1.83	  vs 1.57</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.28	  vs 0.30</p>
<p>    Turnover		  2.73	  vs 2.83</p>
<p>Full name: Oakfields Thoroughbreds and Leisure Industries Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - South African horse breeding and racing group Oakfields said a restructuring had seen it sell most of its racehorses in the year, but that prices obtained for its broodmares were lower than expected due to the depressed state of the industry.</p>
<p>The firm repeated an earlier cautionary announcement due to ongoing talks that may effect its share price.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
